mdns-bridge forwards multicast DNS (Bonjour / DNS-SD) between network
segments so that clients on one VLAN can discover services such as
AirPlay, Google Cast, printers and HomeKit accessories on another.

Unlike a plain mDNS repeater it filters what is forwarded: globally,
per interface in both directions, and per source/destination interface
pair, using allow or deny lists of service labels or host names.

This plugin provides the OPNsense GUI, service control, CARP high
availability support and logging for the mdns-bridge daemon by
Denny Page.

WWW: https://github.com/dennypage/mdns-bridge

# Plugin Changelog

1.0.b1_1

- Only members of wheel and wwwonly may stop the service through
  configd (as OPNsense plugins #5947)
- install.sh registers the plugin with the firmware page

  1.0.b1 (beta)

- Interface check before start: a missing device or an interface that
  would not be bridged (no usable address) stops the start with a message
  naming it, instead of failing silently or bridging only some networks
- When the service does not start, the reason is shown on the settings
  page; the Generated configuration tab shows the interface check
- Replaces os-mdns-bridge-devel builds of 0.1 on installation

  1.0 (development, not released)

- Per-interface inbound and outbound filters, peer-specific outbound
  filters, deny lists and the <all> deny-all filter
- Per-interface IPv4/IPv6 control and optional decode warnings (-w)
- CARP support now depends on one selected CARP VIP
- Apply no longer reports an error on a CARP BACKUP node
- Dedicated log file and a read-only view of the generated configuration
- Restart after an address change on a bridged interface
- Settings from 0.1 are migrated automatically

  0.1

- Initial release
